{"name":"Loft Space","hex":"#cbcecd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"loft","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Air, the air; the sky, the heavens.","An attic or similar space (often used for storage) in the roof of a house or other building.\nSuch an attic used as an atelier."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To propel high into the air.","To fly or travel through the air, as though propelled"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loft"},{"term":"space","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Unlimited or generalized extent, physical or otherwise.\nThe distance between objects. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The distance between objects. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To roam, walk, wander.","To set some distance apart."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/space"}],"entries":[{"title":"Loft","blocks":[{"text":"A loft is a building's upper storey or elevated area in a room directly under the roof, or just an attic: a storage space under the roof usually accessed by a ladder. A loft apartment refers to large adaptable open space, often converted for residential use from some other use, often light industrial."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/400SGreenLoft.jpg/330px-400SGreenLoft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loft","wikidata":"Q620861"},{"title":"Space","blocks":[{"text":"Space is a three-dimensional continuum containing positions and directions. In classical physics, physical space is often conceived in three linear dimensions. Modern physicists usually consider it, with time, to be part of a boundless four-dimensional continuum known as spacetime. The concept of space is considered to be of fundamental importance to an understanding of the physical universe. However, disagreement continues between philosophers over whether it is itself an entity, a relationship between entities, or part of a conceptual framework."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/3D_coordinate_system.svg/330px-3D_coordinate_system.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space","wikidata":"Q107"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Cabins_with_Loft.jpg/500px-Cabins_with_Loft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Cabins_with_Loft.jpg/500px-Cabins_with_Loft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A US-style loft; the additional story covers only a few rooms, leaving one or more sides open to the lower floor","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACabins_with_Loft.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/A_LOFT_IN_SAO_PAULO_CITY.jpg/500px-A_LOFT_IN_SAO_PAULO_CITY.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/A_LOFT_IN_SAO_PAULO_CITY.jpg/1280px-A_LOFT_IN_SAO_PAULO_CITY.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/A_LOFT_IN_SAO_PAULO_CITY.jpg/500px-A_LOFT_IN_SAO_PAULO_CITY.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alto de Santana, São Paulo, Brazil.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_LOFT_IN_SAO_PAULO_CITY.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Cotton%27s_Gardens.jpg/500px-Cotton%27s_Gardens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Cotton%27s_Gardens.jpg/1280px-Cotton%27s_Gardens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&